    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8599a252",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts chimpanzees, which are non-human primates, with overlaid text that anthropomorphizes one of them as 'Harold, the oldest of all the apes,' and describes a fictional escape scenario. While the meme is presented as humorous, it relies on the longstanding and harmful stereotype of equating Black people with apes, which is a form of anti-Black racism. This stereotype dehumanizes Black individuals by reducing them to a primitive, animalistic state, reinforcing racist ideologies and perpetuating systemic discrimination. The meme's intent is to elicit laughter through absurdity, but it does so by invoking a deeply offensive and historically rooted racist trope. The juxtaposition of the image of chimpanzees with the text about 'the oldest of all the apes' is a direct analogical mapping that leverages the racist association between Black people and apes to create a joke, which is inherently harmful due to its reliance on racialized dehumanization. The meme's overall intent is to entertain by exploiting a harmful racial stereotype, thereby contributing to the normalization and perpetuation of anti-Black racism.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2192ebf5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
